(M4, M5)\n2067:            (sections 7.4.1 and 7.4.3; 7.5.1 marker keys\n2083:          :store-of consult and its frame threading (7.3).\n2094:## 11. Completion criteria\n2110:5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n2131:12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n2132:    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, section\n2134:    key, and the re-sealed references of section 7.3, sections 7.5.1,\n2136:    7.3 and the resource decode targets and store model it moves\n2279:  manifests or a single image per format is undecided; section 7.4\n2284:  (section 6.3). Whether `yin.repl` adopts the `dao.jing.remote` timing\n2285:  options, `dao.lease`, or its own is an M5 decision.\n2290:  amendment to UCF section 7.3.2 and `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section\n2294:  boundary (section 6.1). A portable, non-blocking DHT client that could\n2302:  module-store instance (section 7.3), so writes never cross tasks. A\n2332:|                                   | (7.3 sealed references; export    |\n2360:|                                   | (7.3 sealed references; UCF 7.5.1 |\n2402:|                                   | reference (7.3 resource lowering).|\n2427:|                                   | (7.3 private engine resources,    |\n2440:|                                   | before (7.3 walker rule,          |\n2462:|                                   | (7.3 grow-only returns, criterion |\n2480:|                                   | instance (7.3 module store,       |\n2489:|                                   | (7.3 walker rule, criterion 23).  |\n2527:|                                   | coordinates (7.3 acts 3-4, 8.3). |\n2538:|                                   | module grain (7.3, 8.3).          |\n2560:| Scalar id in `:link-response`     | Agreed. Now `[:t0 7]` (7.2).      |\n2571:|                                   | the lift (7.3).                   |\n2594:| Two scalar id examples left       | Agree