{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1130,1245p'; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1130\t   interpreter, run the parked VM, and either answer its value -- the\n  1131\t   round the require began in finally completes -- report it pending\n  1132\t   again, or, when the re-check raised the link's refusal, return the\n  1133\t   shell to the round's base with the error as text.\"\n  1134\t  [state]\n  1135\t  (let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1136\t    (try\n  1137\t      (let [[state' vm' pending] (drive-links state (:vm parked))]\n  1138\t        (if (vm/halted? vm')\n  1139\t          (let [vm'' (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:base parked)) vm')\n  1140\t                [st text] (finalize-eval state\n  1141\t                                         (assoc state' :vm vm'')\n  1142\t                                         (tokenize state' vm''))]\n  1143\t            [(assoc st :vm vm'' :pending-run nil) text])\n  1144\t          (let [[st text] (drain-output state')]\n  1145\t            [(assoc st\n  1146\t                    :vm vm'\n  1147\t                    :pending-run (assoc parked :vm vm' :links pending))\n  1148\t             (str text (pending-text pending))])))\n  1149\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  1150\t        (let [[st text] (drain-output state)]\n  1151\t          [(assoc st\n  1152\t                  :vm (carry-link-counter (:base parked) (:vm parked))\n  1153\t                  :pending-run nil)\n  1154\t           (str text (format-error error))])))))\n  1155\t\n  1156\t\n  1157\t(defn- command-line?\n  1158\t  [parsed]\n  1159\t  (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n  1160\t        form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n  1161\t    (and form (command-form? form))))\n  1162\t\n  1163\t\n  1164\t(defn- eval-parsed\n  1165\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1166\t  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n  1167\t    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n  1168\t    ;; pending the line is consumed with the notice -- the parked VM owns\n  1169\t    ;; the store a new evaluation would fork -- and once it completes the\n  1170\t    ;; line evaluates against the completed state.\n  1171\t    (let [[state' text] (resume-pending state)]\n  1172\t      (if (:pending-run state')\n  1173\t        [state' text]\n  1174\t        (let [[state'' text2] (eval-parsed* state' trimmed parsed)]\n  1175\t          [state'' (str text \"\\n\" text2)])))\n  1176\t    (eval-parsed* state trimmed parsed)))\n  1177\t\n  1178\t\n  1179\t(defn eval-input\n  1180\t  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n  1181\t\n  1182\t   Input whose brackets do not balance is retained as `:pending-input` and\n  1183\t   produces no text.  Nothing here is asynchronous: the driver, not this\n  1184\t   namespace, decides when the next step happens.\"\n  1185\t  [state line]\n  1186\t  (let [pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n  1187\t        combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n  1188\t                   (str/trim line)\n  1189\t                   (str pending \"\\n\" (str/trim line)))]\n  1190\t    (if (pos? (bracket-balance combined))\n  1191\t      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n  1192\t      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n  1193\t            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n  1194\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n  1195\t                                  :clj Exception\n  1196\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n  1197\t                          {:error error}))]\n  1198\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n  1199\t\n  1200\t\n  1201\t(defn repl-state\n  1202\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n  1203\t\n  1204\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n  1205\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n  1206\t   operation.\n  1207\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n  1208\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n  1209\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n  1210\t   further evaluation.  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n  1211\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).\"\n  1212\t  [state]\n  1213\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n  1214\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n  1215\t                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n  1216\t                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n  1217\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n  1218\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n  1219\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n  1220\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n  1221\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n  1222\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n  1223\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n  1224\t   :running? (:running? state)\n  1225\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n  1226\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n  1227\t   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1228\t              (mapv (fn [p]\n  1229\t                      {:name (:name p)\n  1230\t                       :link-id (:yin.link/id p)})\n  1231\t                    (:links parked)))\n  1232\t   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n  1233\t   :remote {:connected? false}})\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker\n     2\t  \"The code linker (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md): fetches and verifies\n     3\t   code over a DaoStream content pair (section 6). The linker holds no\n     4\t   DaoJing handle: every read is a `:jing/get-content` request on a\n     5\t   `dao.stream.rpc` client, answered by whatever serves the pair -- a\n     6\t   local store, a `dao.jing.dht/create-content-dht` handle, or a remote\n     7\t   endpoint -- behind `dao.jing.remote/default-handlers`.\n     8\t\n     9\t   The portable interface is stepped (section 6.3): `link-state`,\n    10\t   `request-link`, `step`, and `abandon` are pure functions over explicit\n    11\t   state. `fetch` is host policy over a link runtime (section 6.4): it\n    12\t   drives one link to its completion and runs step 5b against the\n    13\t   receiver. `verify` (steps 3 to 5a) and `discharge` (step 5b) are the\n    14\t   pure checks over values already in hand.\n    15\t\n    16\t   One format-neutral admission-then-six-step pipeline serves every\n    17\t   format (sections 4.1-4.2). A format record supplies the contract, the\n    18\t   identity mint and match, the row-local validator, the whole-value\n    19\t   validator, the three position-bearing scanners of section 4.1\n    20\t   (`:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, `:applications-fn`), and the\n    21\t   parts worklist; the four records are `ast-format`, `semantic-format`,\n    22\t   `stack-format`, and `register-format` (section 5). The manifest and\n    23\t   derivation record formats of section 8.1 are `manifest-format` and\n    24\t   `record-format`, and `link-manifest` is the manifest-delivered image\n    25\t   link. Storage\n    26\t   addresses (`jing/segment-key`) and VM identities (H, R) are separate\n    27\t   preimages for the de Bruijn formats and the same preimage for the\n    28\t   storage-derived ones, so step 2 checks the address and step 3 checks\n    29\t   the identity; neither subsumes the other (I5).\n    30\t\n    31\t   The rpc client, the indexes, the format records, and the bounds are\n    32\t   linker-local state (section 6.2); the receiver environment is an\n    33\t   explicit argument. There is no global loader, registry, callback, or\n    34\t   cache here, and every outcome -- success or refusal -- is a returned\n    35\t   plain data map (section 4.3).\"\n    36\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n    37\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    38\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    39\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    40\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply]\n    41\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    42\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    43\t            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n    44\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as debruijn-code]\n    45\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as linearize]\n    46\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as debruijn-register-code]\n    47\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as register-compile]\n    48\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-resolve :as resolve]\n    49\t            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n    50\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t;; =============================================================================\n    54\t;; Refusal vocabulary (section 4.3)\n    55\t;; =============================================================================\n    56\t\n    57\t(def refusal-reasons\n    58\t  \"Every reason a linker refusal may carry.\"\n    59\t  #{:invalid-request :absent :address-mismatch :hash-mismatch\n    60\t    :descriptor-defect :parts-limit :contract-mismatch :use-before-definition\n    61\t    :unresolved-free :shadowed-free :unsupported-format :pairing-mismatch\n    62\t    :undeclared-free :module-name-mismatch :derivation-mismatch\n    63\t    :unverified-derivation})\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn refused\n    67\t  \"A qualified refusal: `{:status :refused, :reason reason}` merged with\n    68\t   the step's own evidence `data`.\"\n    69\t  ([reason] (refused reason {}))\n    70\t  ([reason data]\n    71\t   (merge data {:status :refused, :reason reason})))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn refused?\n    75\t  \"True when `res` is a linker refusal.\"\n    76\t  [res]\n    77\t  (and (map? res) (= :refused (:status res))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn ok?\n    81\t  \"True when `res` is a verified linker outcome.\"\n    82\t  [res]\n    83\t  (and (map? res) (= :ok (:status res))))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t;; =============================================================================\n    87\t;; Free-name scanners (sections 5.1, 5.2)\n    88\t;; =============================================================================\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- distinct-names\n    91\t  [names]\n    92\t  (vec (distinct names)))\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn stack-free-names\n    96\t  \"Every `:load-free` name in a canonical stack instruction vector, in pc\n    97\t   order of first appearance.\"\n    98\t  [instruction-vector]\n    99\t  (distinct-names\n   100\t    (keep (fn [t] (when (= :load-free (nth t 0)) (nth t 1)))\n   101\t          instruction-vector)))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn register-free-names\n   105\t  \"Every `:load-free` name across all bodies of a register image map, in\n   106\t   pc order of first appearance. A register `:load-free` is\n   107\t   `[:load-free rd name]`.\"\n   108\t  [register-image-map]\n   109\t  (distinct-names\n   110\t    (keep (fn [t] (when (= :load-free (nth t 0)) (nth t 2)))\n   111\t          (:instructions register-image-map))))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn- all-var-names\n   115\t  \"The conservative fallback for a vector whose layout the scope walk\n   116\t   cannot read: every `:var` name, all free. Over-approximating\n   117\t   obligations is always admissible.\"\n   118\t  [v]\n   119\t  (set (keep (fn [t]\n   120\t               (when (and (vector? t)\n   121\t                          (= :var (nth t 0))\n   122\t                          (< 1 (count t)))\n   123\t                 (nth t 1)))\n   124\t             v)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- closure-spans\n   128\t  \"`[[c body r] ...]` for every `:closure` of canonical vector `v`: the\n   129\t   body of the closure at pc `c` is `[body r]`, `r` the first `:return`\n   130\t   at or after `body` (the out-of-line bodies of UCF section 7.3.2); nil\n   131\t   `r` when there is none.\"\n   132\t  [v]\n   133\t  (let [n (count v)]\n   134\t    (keep (fn [c]\n   135\t            (let [t (nth v c)]\n   136\t              (when (and (vector? t)\n   137\t                         (= :closure (nth t 0))\n   138\t                         (< 2 (count t)))\n   139\t                (let [body (nth t 2)]\n   140\t                  [c body\n   141\t                   (first (filter (fn [pc]\n   142\t                                    (let [u (nth v pc)]\n   143\t                                      (and (vector? u)\n   144\t                                           (= :return (nth u 0)))))\n   145\t                                  (range body n)))]))))\n   146\t          (range n))))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn- spans-conform?\n   150\t  \"Whether `spans` is the closed, off-pc-0, pairwise-disjoint body layout\n   151\t   the scope walk reads; anything else rules every `:var` free.\"\n   152\t  [spans]\n   153\t  (let [pairs (map (fn [[_ b r]] [b r]) spans)]\n   154\t    (and (every? (fn [[b r]] (and r (pos? b))) pairs)\n   155\t         (= (count pairs) (count (distinct pairs)))\n   156\t         (every? (fn [[[b1 r1] [b2 r2]]] (or (< r1 b2) (< r2 b1)))\n   157\t                 (for [x pairs, y pairs :when (neg? (compare x y))]\n   158\t                   [x y])))))\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn- vector-layout\n   162\t  \"The closure body spans of canonical vector `v` when they are the\n   163\t   closed, off-pc-0, pairwise-disjoint layout the scope walk reads, else\n   164\t   nil -- every scanner then degrades (section 4.1).\"\n   165\t  [v]\n   166\t  (let [spans (closure-spans v)]\n   167\t    (when (spans-conform? spans) spans)))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- safe-layout\n   171\t  \"Like `vector-layout`, but a vector the walk cannot read at all (an\n   172\t   operand that throws) degrades too.\"\n   173\t  [v]\n   174\t  (try (vector-layout v)\n   175\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(defn- in-body-pc?\n   179\t  \"Whether pc `p` lies in one of the closure body spans `spans`.\"\n   180\t  [spans p]\n   181\t  (boolean (some (fn [[_ b r]] (<= b p r)) spans)))\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\t(defn- conditional-ranges\n   185\t  \"The pcs a conditional target range covers in canonical vector `v`\n   186\t   (section 4.1): for every `:jump` or `:branch-false` at pc b with\n   187\t   target t, the pcs strictly between b and t, either direction -- the\n   188\t   fall-through a taken branch skips, and a backward jump's body.\"\n   189\t  [v]\n   190\t  (into #{}\n   191\t        (mapcat (fn [[b t]]\n   192\t                  (when (and (integer? t) (not= b t))\n   193\t                    (range (inc (min b t)) (max b t)))))\n   194\t        (keep (fn [pc]\n   195\t                (let [t (nth v pc)]\n   196\t                  (when (and (vector? t)\n   197\t                             (contains? #{:jump :branch-false}\n   198\t                                        (nth t 0)))\n   199\t                    [pc (nth t 1)])))\n   200\t              (range (count v)))))\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\t(defn- degraded-occurrences\n   204\t  \"The conservative degradation's own occurrence records (section 4.1):\n   205\t   every name retained at no position, inside a body -- a scanner that\n   206\t   cannot read positions retains every occurrence and discharges\n   207\t   nothing.\"\n   208\t  [names]\n   209\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   210\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :in-body? true}) names))))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn- degraded-definitions\n   214\t  \"The conservative degradation's own definition records (section 4.1):\n   215\t   every key retained at no position, conditional -- a definition whose\n   216\t   position is unknown discharges nothing.\"\n   217\t  [names]\n   218\t  (vec (sort-by (comp str :name)\n   219\t                (map (fn [n] {:name n, :at nil, :conditional? true})\n   220\t                     names))))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t(defn semantic-free-occurrences\n   224\t  \"Every free `:var` occurrence of canonical vector `v` as a section 4.1\n   225\t   record `{:name sym :at pc :in-body? b}`, in pc order (UCF section\n   226\t   7.3.2): a `:var` at pc `p` is bound iff `p` lies in the body of a\n   227\t   `:closure` whose params hold the name, transitively through the body\n   228\t   holding that closure's own pc. Over a vector whose body spans are not\n   229\t   closed, off pc 0, and pairwise disjoint -- anything but the\n   230\t   ast-to-bytecode layout -- every `:var` name degrades to a record with\n   231\t   no position: over-approximating obligations is always admissible.\"\n   232\t  [v]\n   233\t  (try\n   234\t    (if-let [spans (vector-layout v)]\n   235\t      (let [params (into {}\n   236\t                         (keep (fn [c]\n   237\t                                 (let [t (nth v c)]\n   238\t                                   (when (and (vector? t)\n   239\t                                              (= :closure (nth t 0)))\n   240\t                                     [c (nth t 1)]))))\n   241\t                         (range (count v)))\n   242\t            owner (fn [pc]\n   243\t                    (some (fn [[c b r]] (when (<= b pc r) c)) spans))\n   244\t            bound? (fn bound?\n   245\t                     [pc sym]\n   246\t                     (when-let [c (owner pc)]\n   247\t                       (or (some #(= % sym) (get params c))\n   248\t                           (bound? c sym))))]\n   249\t        (vec (keep (fn [pc]\n   250\t                     (let [t (nth v pc)]\n   251\t                       (when (and (vector? t)\n   252\t                                  (= :var (nth t 0))\n   253\t                                  (< 1 (count t))\n   254\t                                  (not (bound? pc (nth t 1))))\n   255\t                         {:name (nth t 1), :at pc,\n   256\t                          :in-body? (in-body-pc? spans pc)})))\n   257\t                   (range (count v)))))\n   258\t      (degraded-occurrences (all-var-names v)))\n   259\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   260\t      (degraded-occurrences (all-var-names v)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
