age` attached by the kernel's `attach-image` under its\n   343\t     own contract; an image already held is not attached twice.\")\n   344\t\n   345\t  (lift-closure\n   346\t    [vm closure encode]\n   347\t    \"The `:yin.k/closure` marker of `closure` in `vm`'s coordinates,\n   348\t     captured values encoded by `encode`, with `:yin.k/store-of` when the\n   349\t     closure carries one. Throws the `:yin.k/non-portable` refusal as\n   350\t     ex-data when the closure cannot be lifted.\")\n   351\t\n   352\t  (lower-closure\n   353\t    [vm marker decode]\n   354\t    \"The closure `marker` denotes in `vm`'s coordinates, captured values\n   355\t     decoded by `decode`, carrying the marker's `:yin.k/store-of`. A\n   356\t     marker of another binding discipline or format is\n   357\t     `:binding-mismatch`.\"))\n   358\t\n  1080\t   `[state refusal]`.\"\n  1081\t  [state module-name response link-id]\n  1082\t  (try\n  1083\t    (let [[child state] (spawn-child state module-name response)]\n  1084\t      [(assoc-in state [:installs module-name]\n  1085\t                 {:phase :running, :vm child, :parent link-id,\n  1086\t                  :response response})\n  1087\t       nil])\n  1088\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n  1089\t      [state (assoc (error-refusal module-name e) :phase :loading)])))\n  1090\t\n  1091\t\n  1092\t(defn- settle\n  1093\t  \"Act on the response correlated with `entry`: a refusal (or loss) is\n  1094\t   raised as the effect's error; `:ok` runs step 5b against the live\n  1095\t   state and, discharged, starts the install child, the entry becoming\n  1096\t   an `:install` waiter. A module linked or installing meanwhile answers\n  1097\t   or joins instead, and a manifest naming another module than the one\n  1098\t   required is `:module-name-mismatch`, never installed. Returns `[state\n  1099\t   waiting woken]`.\"\n  1100\t  [state entry response]\n  1101\t  (let [state (retire state (:link-id entry) :restored)\n  1102\t        module-name (:name entry)\n  1103\t        waiter (-> entry\n  1104\t                   (dissoc :envelope :request :response :cursor :link-id)\n  1105\t                   (assoc :reason :install))]\n  1106\t    (cond\n  1107\t      (not= :ok (:status response))\n  1108\t      [state nil (refused-entry entry response)]\n  1109\t\n  1110\t      (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n  1111\t      [state nil (ready entry module-name)]\n  1112\t\n  1113\t      (contains? (:installs state) module-name) [state waiter nil]\n  1114\t\n  1115\t      ;; the linker checks the name (section 8.1); a response that names\n  1116\t      ;; another module is never installed under this one\n  1117\t      (not= module-name (get-in response [:manifest :yin.module/name]))\n  1118\t      [state nil\n  1119\t       (refused-entry entry\n  1120\t                      (linker/refused :module-name-mismatch\n  1121\t                                      {:requested module-name,\n  1122\t                                       :manifest (get-in\n  1123\t                                                   response\n  1124\t                                                   [:manifest\n  1125\t                                                    :yin.module/name])}))]\n  1126\t\n  1127\t      :else\n  1128\t      (if-let [refusal (discharge-defect state response)]\n  1129\t        [state nil (refused-entry entry refusal)]\n  1130\t        (let [[state refusal] (start-install state module-name response\n  1131\t                                             (:link-id entry))]\n  1132\t          (if refusal\n  1133\t            [state nil (refused-entry entry refusal)]\n  1134\t            [state waiter nil]))))))\n  1135\t\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:61:   A reserved name (Rule R: `yin/def` is syntax, never a name) is refused\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:844:(defn- discharge-