{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"## M5 commit gate\n\n**Verdict: REJECT.** The supplied JVM, Node, Dart, cljstyle, and kondo results are clean. I did not rerun them. The diff still has rollback and pending-state defects that the current tests do not cover.\n\n### Findings\n\n- **P0 — Rolled-back child origins can be reused on the same link pair.** An install child gets its origin from the parent’s `:origins` counter ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:920)). On failure or `(abandon)`, the shell restores the round’s base VM and carries only `:id-counter` ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:799), [repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1068)). The link pair survives that rollback. A later install can therefore mint the same child origin and link ID; a late response to the old child can settle the later require. The fix must preserve *all* identity generation used on the surviving pair, including `:origins`, across every rollback, or replace the pair.\n\n- **P1 — The failure path can also lose newly minted root IDs.** `run-evaluation` snapshots `floor` before `drive-links` and restores that snapshot if driving throws ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:902)). `resume-pending` restores the previously parked VM if driving throws ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1135)). Either drive may have advanced identity state before the exception. Carry the latest VM identity state, rather than the pre-drive snapshot, when retaining the pair.\n\n- **P1 — Some pending runs cannot be abandoned as documented.** `(abandon)` retires only IDs in `:pending-run :links` ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1058)). That list comes from requests the interpreter reported pending; it can be empty while the VM waits at `:install` or while a link response is outstanding ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:811), [repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:860)). The command then drops the parked VM without raising the promised abandonment error. Derive abandonment from the VM’s live waits and handle install waits explicitly.\n\n- **P2 — Input is silently consumed while a link remains pending.** A non-command line triggers a recheck; if the require is still pending, that line is discarded ([repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1164)). The test asserts this behavior ([require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:275)). The prompt notice says “another line re-checks it,” but does not tell the user their entered program will be lost. Provide an explicit recheck command, or retain and evaluate the line exactly once when the link completes.\n\n- **P2 — A failed response append is counted as progress.** `serve` leaves its cursor unchanged when `respond!` fails, yet returns `:progress? true` ([link.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:284)). This causes bounded retries and a misleading pending state instead of reporting the response-medium failure.\n\n### Gate checks\n\nThe `:defer-discharge` option is false by default ([linker.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2137)); this composition sets it explicitly ([link.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:207)). The VM discharges a correlated successful response before starting installation ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1092)). I found no path in this wiring that installs the deferred image without that check.\n\nThe test does use one manifest for stack and register sessions, checks distinct H/R identities, and compares B0-normalized results ([require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc:226)). The store-write audit entry is justified: `composition` puts a `dao.jing` byte-store handle in a content-source descriptor ([link.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m5/src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:107)); it does not write the VM program store. I found no new Rule R, external contract-stamp, or ClojureDart reader-conditional violation in the reviewed changes.\n\nFor failure policy, the bounded, clock-free pending state is a reasonable REPL mechanism. Keep `fetch` deadline-free. If the driver later supplies a tick clock and the owner wants a deadline, compose it with `dao.lease`; `dao.jing.remote` timing options concern content transport attempts, not the lifetime of a require.\n\n**Must fix before this gate passes:** preserve unique root and child link identities across every rollback; make `(abandon)` cover every pending phase and raise its error; stop silently discarding program input; report failed response appends accurately. Add targeted regression coverage for late responses after failure and abandonment."}}
